# Visual direction

- Follow `docs/design-references/`, `docs/design-system/`, `UI_ARCHITECTURE.md`, ADR 0003.
- Aesthetic: GeoCities-inspired, dark grid, glitter typography, torn-paper cards, pixel stickers, retro desktop windows, flat-lay board.
- Normal mode: all **enabled** modules visible together.
- Focus mode: selected module lifts; **board stays visible behind**.
- Animation modes: `full` | `reduced` | `disabled`; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Do not ship purple-indigo SaaS gradients, cream/terracotta AI-default looks, or KPI dashboards.
- Do not turn the board into a social feed or poster/infographic as the live UI.

## Before any UI work

1. Inspect relevant images under `docs/design-references/` (open them).
2. Cite those filenames in the implementation report.
3. For screens without a direct reference, use `docs/design-system/` (especially `FOCUS_MODE.md` + `REFERENCE_CATALOG.md`, usually via `01` + `10`).
4. Meet WCAG 2.2 AA (`docs/design-system/ACCESSIBILITY.md`).
5. Preserve flat-lay + focus behavior (`FOCUS_MODE.md`, `RESPONSIVE_BEHAVIOR.md`).
6. Never replace this design with standard dashboard/admin components.
7. Never use a generated reference image as the actual clickable application surface — rebuild with live HTML/CSS/SVG components.
8. Do not copy generated-image mistakes (typos, fake values, garbled text, non-functional chrome).
9. Run `docs/design-system/REFERENCE_COMPLIANCE_CHECKLIST.md` before calling UI work done.
